      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright (c) 2010 John Wiley & Sons, Ltd.",
        "AbstractText": "Latent structure models have been proposed in many applications. For space-time health data it is often important to be able to find the underlying trends in time, which are supported by subsets of small areas. Latent structure modeling is one such approach to this analysis. This paper presents a mixture-based approach that can be applied to component selection. The analysis of a Georgia ambulatory asthma county-level data set is presented and a simulation-based evaluation is made."
      },
